<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	The whole of this tweak's settings page, and no code of its own.

	A preference bundle is a Mach-O that Settings loads with dlopen, and this tweak
	is built on a Linux toolchain whose arm64e output the loader on an A12 or newer
	device does not fix up properly. Nothing about that is visible until the objc
	runtime walks the classes in the newly loaded image, reads a pointer that was
	never rebased, and takes Settings down with it - which is what every build up to
	1.4.8 did the moment this row was tapped.

	Settings can build a page out of a plist on its own, so it does. "entry" is the
	row that appears in the Settings list; an entry with no bundle behind it is one
	PreferenceLoader owns, and the page it pushes is the "items" below, read by a
	controller inside PreferenceLoader itself. Every value is read and written
	straight into the tweak's own preference domain and posts the notification
	SpringBoard reloads on, so there is nothing left for a bundle to do here - and
	nothing of this tweak's inside Settings that could crash it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>entry</key>
	<dict>
		<key>cell</key>
		<string>PSLinkCell</string>
		<key>icon</key>
